@end menu

@node gpui-au User Guide
@section User Guide

End users do not interact with this crate directly. It is responsible
for the editor windows that appear when a SotF plugin is instantiated
as an Audio Unit. Symptoms relevant to users:

@itemize @bullet
@item Editor window appears empty: usually means
  @code{gpui_au_request_frame} is not being called by the Swift host
  (CADisplayLink/timer issue).
@item Mouse/keyboard events not forwarded: AUv3 sandboxing, see the
  developer guide.
@end itemize

@node gpui-au Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading How it works

@example
Swift AUViewController
  └── NSView (host-provided)
       └── CAMetalLayer
            └── wgpu (Metal backend)
                 └── GPUI rendering
@end example

@enumerate
@item Swift creates an @code{AUViewController} with an
  @code{NSView}.
@item Rust @code{AuPlatform} initialises GPUI against that external
  @code{NSView}.
@item Swift calls @code{gpui_au_request_frame()} per display refresh.
@item Mouse/keyboard events are forwarded
  @code{NSView -> FFI -> GPUI}.
@end enumerate

@subheading Key entry points

@table @code
@item gpui_au_init
Initialise the GPUI platform against an external NSView pointer.
@item gpui_au_request_frame
Pump one render frame; driven by Swift CVDisplayLink / timer.
@item gpui_au_forward_event
Push a Cocoa event into the GPUI dispatcher.
@end table

@subheading Notes

@itemize @bullet
@item AUv3 sandbox forbids window creation; that is why an external
  NSView is required.
@item CoreText is used for text rendering to match Apple HIG.
@item Display-driven rendering avoids spinning a redraw loop when the
  plugin is idle.
@end itemize
